# Local backend — active. Needs `npm run dev` in backend/ (or `make up`) and the
# phone on this same Wi-Fi. 8002 is the dev port used by backend/.env,
# docker-compose and the Makefile — NOT 8001, which is redis-insight.
# Physical device: this laptop's LAN IP (`hostname -I` to re-check):
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.110.9:8002/api/v1
# Android emulator instead (10.0.2.2 maps to this machine's localhost):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8002/api/v1

# Deployed backend on Render — works on any network (mobile data included) and
# is HTTPS, which Android *release* builds require (cleartext HTTP is blocked by
# default since Android 9; the debug manifest allows it, so the dev APK is fine
# with the plain-HTTP LAN URL above).
# Currently NOT RESPONDING: TLS connects, then zero bytes back until timeout.
# Redeploy / wake the Render service before switching back to this line.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://tempu-6.onrender.com/api/v1

# Old laptops / IPs:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.0.124:8001/api/v1
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.200.202:8000/api/v1
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.136.132:5000/api/v1

# Native Google Maps SDK key for the MapView (screens/home/Map.js uses
# PROVIDER_GOOGLE). Without this the map renders as a blank white grid.
# Get one at console.cloud.google.com → enable "Maps SDK for Android"
# (and "Maps SDK for iOS" for iOS). Injected via app.config.js at build time.
# Re-run `npx expo prebuild --clean` after changing this.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=AIzaSyBOldlugWhnruhmr2Bh_IZhg15u4H4jH3k